  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-13T17:53:55.886Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "(Originally posted as a bug report — it turns out \"Request Invite\" was never available for friends in joinable instances. Reframing this as a feature request. Moderators, please move this to Feature Requests if possible.)\n\nCurrently, when a friend is in a joinable instance (Friends / Friends+), only \"Join\" is shown on their user page. I'd like to be able to send a Request Invite in this situation as well.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nEven when an instance is technically joinable, many users would prefer to ask \"is now a good time to join?\" instead of jumping in directly. This kind of etiquette is especially well-established in the Japanese community.\n\nThe friend may be in the middle of a conversation, an event, or taking photos. There are many situations where you want to check whether it's okay to join right now — for example, to avoid running into someone you'd rather not meet who happens to be in the same instance.\n\n## Suggestion\n\nShow both \"Join\" and \"Request Invite\" when a friend is in a joinable instance, and let the friend accept (or ignore) the request as usual.",
